# A6L debug / first-install kernel fragment (r6b boot fix, 30 Sep 2026, docs/rom-r6b-bootfix-20260930.md).
# Applied ON TOP of the r5 thermal config (firmware/extracted/kernel-r5-20260930/config) for the r6b userdebug / first-install
# kernel ONLY (kernel-r5p-20260930). A kCFI type mismatch then logs "CFI failure at ..." with a backtrace (WARN) and the call
# continues, instead of the BRK trap -> oops -> the task dies holding its locks (device_lock / component / drm locks), which
# hangs every later insmod of the display group silently.
# Module ABI neutral: CFI_PERMISSIVE only changes the trap handler in vmlinux (Module.symvers byte-identical, checked by
# build-r5p.sh), so the staged r5 modules load unchanged.
# RELEASE keeps strict kCFI: a6l-release.config has "# CONFIG_CFI_PERMISSIVE is not set".
CONFIG_CFI_PERMISSIVE=y
